.TH IREE-ROCKET-RUN-MODULE 1 "November 2026" "iree-rocket" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iree-rocket-run-module \- IREE's iree-run-module with the Rocket NPU driver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iree-rocket-run-module
.BI \-\-module= MODULE.vmfb
.BI \-\-function= NAME
.BR \-\-device=rocket " " \-\-device=local\-task
[\fB\-\-input=\fIINPUT\fR...]
[\fIOPTION\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
IREE's
.B iree-run-module
built with the Rocket HAL driver for the RK3588 NPU linked in, and renamed so
it cannot collide with an upstream IREE installation. It runs one function of
a .vmfb module and prints its results.
.PP
Modules from
.BR rocket-compiler (1)
place their work on two devices, so pass both, in this order:
.B \-\-device=rocket \-\-device=local\-task
.PP
Run it with
.B \-\-help
for the full list of IREE's options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /dev/accel/accel0
The NPU, through the mainline rocket kernel driver. Opening it needs read and
write access, which Debian gives the
.B render
group.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rocket-run-module (1),
.BR iree-rocket-benchmark-module (1),
.BR rocket-compiler (1)
